{"name":"Floriography","hex":"#a54049","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"floriography","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Communication through the use of flowers, with different types of flowers having particular symbolic meanings."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/floriography"}],"entries":[{"title":"Floriography (album)","blocks":[{"text":"Floriography is the debut studio album released by Norwegian musician Moddi. The album was released on 8 February 2010 through Propeller Recordings in Norway. The album peaked at number nine on the Norwegian Albums Charts. The album includes the single \"Ardennes\" and \"Smoke\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/a/a6/Moddi_Floriography.jpg/330px-Moddi_Floriography.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Floriography_(album)"},{"title":"Language of flowers","blocks":[{"text":"Floriography is a means of cryptological communication through the use or arrangement of flowers. Meaning has been attributed to flowers for thousands of years, and some form of floriography has been practiced in traditional cultures throughout Europe, Asia, and Africa."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/%27Language_of_Flowers%27_by_Alphonse_Mucha.jpg/330px-%27Language_of_Flowers%27_by_Alphonse_Mucha.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Language_of_flowers"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/Floral_poetry_and_the_language_of_flowers_%281877%29_%2814782868105%29.jpg/500px-Floral_poetry_and_the_language_of_flowers_%281877%29_%2814782868105%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/Floral_poetry_and_the_language_of_flowers_%281877%29_%2814782868105%29.jpg/1280px-Floral_poet